<h2>Primary Command Workflows</h2>

<h3>1. <code>encode</code> — Single and Batch Transcoding</h3>

{{ terminalFrame({
  title: "bash — encode workflow examples",
  stream: "stdout",
  exitCode: 0,
  code: "# Plan and execute an HEVC hardware encode with automatic fallback
flux encode --input raw/interview.mov --output out/interview.mp4 --hardware nvidia --codec hevc --quality balanced

# Dry-run inspection: probe source and print exact FFmpeg ArgumentList without writing files
flux encode --input raw/interview.mov --codec av1 --quality high --dry-run

# Machine-readable JSON output on stdout (human progress and notices stay on stderr)
flux encode --input raw/interview.mov --output out/interview.mkv --codec hevc --json"
}) }}

<h3>2. Option Precedence & Settings Merge</h3>
<p>
  For <code>encode</code> invocations, <code>SettingsMerge</code> resolves configuration in strict priority order:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Explicit command-line flags</strong> passed to the current invocation always win.</li>
  <li><strong>Named preset values</strong> from <code>--preset &lt;name&gt;</code> in <code>settings.json</code> apply next.</li>
  <li><strong>User encode defaults</strong> in <code>settings.json</code> (<code>encode.*</code>) apply unless <code>--no-config</code> is passed.</li>
  <li><strong>Built-in command defaults</strong> apply last.</li>
</ol>
<p>
  Execution-scoped flags (<code>--output</code>, <code>--dry-run</code>, <code>--json</code>, <code>--preset</code>, <code>--no-config</code>) are never read from presets or defaults.
</p>

<h3>3. <code>apply</code> — Declarative Fluxfile Execution</h3>

{{ terminalFrame({
  title: "bash — apply workflow examples",
  stream: "stdout",
  exitCode: 0,
  code: "# Validate syntax, schema, variable references, and DAG cycles offline (no FFmpeg required)
flux apply --check

# Probe existing inputs and print planned FFmpeg commands in dependency order
flux apply --dry-run

# Execute all jobs or a specific target subgraph with variables
flux apply --job web --var EDITION=directors-cut"
}) }}

